WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.110 --> 00:09.030
Could you please take Ms. Minamida off the case going forward?

3
00:09.114 --> 00:10.698
I don't mind.

4
00:10.782 --> 00:12.283
I can't help…

5
00:12.367 --> 00:13.868
the defendant.

6
00:14.661 --> 00:16.329
Ms. Minamida…

7
00:17.330 --> 00:19.707
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

8
00:30.510 --> 00:31.761
It's been three days?

9
00:31.845 --> 00:33.388
Four days.

10
00:48.194 --> 00:49.362
ATTORNEY MINAMI MINAMIDA

11
00:49.445 --> 00:52.240
MS. MINAMIDA, ARE YOU OFF TODAY? HAVEN'T HEARD FROM YOU. ARE YOU OKAY?

12
00:59.747 --> 01:03.918
HOUSE-ROASTED COFFEE

13
01:15.305 --> 01:19.058
Is this really your old, run-down family home, Ririi?

14
01:19.142 --> 01:20.643
We figured we'd make the most

15
01:20.727 --> 01:23.479
of its age and wear when turning it into a cafe.

16
01:23.563 --> 01:26.858
You're opening next month? I'm envious.

17
01:26.941 --> 01:30.945
Retiring and opening a cafe in an old house, just the way you want it.

18
01:31.029 --> 01:32.447
It's always been my dream.

19
01:32.530 --> 01:35.366
I got carried away with the details, so money's a little tight.

20
01:35.450 --> 01:39.287
These are trial dishes. Help yourselves.

21
01:40.288 --> 01:45.043
We have anmitsu and milk jelly, both made with agar.

22
01:45.126 --> 01:47.545
And soft red bean jelly made with agar.

23
01:47.629 --> 01:52.383
And seaweed jelly noodles with mozuku seaweed or vinegar-miso sauce.

24
01:52.467 --> 01:53.885
Agar in everything!

25
01:53.968 --> 01:56.721
The Madokas' agar is homemade by Ririi's mother.

26
01:57.305 --> 01:58.473
Well, time to dig in.

27
02:01.768 --> 02:03.144
Delicious!

28
02:03.228 --> 02:05.480
Great desserts in a beautiful setting.

29
02:05.563 --> 02:07.065
What could be better?

30
02:07.148 --> 02:07.982
Right?

31
02:12.111 --> 02:14.239
If only that weren't there…

32
02:17.533 --> 02:19.535
That storage shed's been there forever.

33
02:20.203 --> 02:21.454
Why not get rid of it?

34
02:21.996 --> 02:23.248
We can't.

35
02:23.331 --> 02:24.874
The land is ours,

36
02:24.958 --> 02:26.542
but the shed belongs to a neighbor.

37
02:27.043 --> 02:29.379
There used to be a construction company behind us.

38
02:29.462 --> 02:33.091
It started using the space to store materials temporarily.

39
02:34.175 --> 02:37.053
The owner died four years ago.

40
02:37.136 --> 02:39.097
When we wanted it removed,

41
02:39.180 --> 02:41.099
we didn't even know who to contact.

42
02:42.016 --> 02:45.812
So your land is being occupied unlawfully?

43
02:45.895 --> 02:47.689
Exactly! Unlawful occupation!

44
02:53.903 --> 02:55.196
She quit?

45
03:01.953 --> 03:03.871
She was taken off a case.

46
03:04.497 --> 03:06.416
I think it shook her confidence.

47
03:06.499 --> 03:08.167
You should've told me.

48
03:12.296 --> 03:13.881
I know.

49
03:13.965 --> 03:15.800
I've got a great idea.

50
03:16.759 --> 03:18.970
I'll get Minami back on her feet.

51
03:19.053 --> 03:20.179
Help me out, Mr. Minamida.

52
03:24.183 --> 03:26.853
I asked around. It depends on what's stored inside,

53
03:26.936 --> 03:30.398
but tearing it down and disposing of it will cost at least 500,000 yen.

54
03:30.481 --> 03:35.403
Five hundred thousand is a lot right after a renovation.

55
03:36.029 --> 03:36.863
Right, Minami?

56
03:38.239 --> 03:39.741
This roof is handy

57
03:39.824 --> 03:41.868
for drying agar, though.

58
03:41.951 --> 03:43.119
Forget about agar for now.

59
03:43.202 --> 03:44.996
We'll discuss agar later.

60
03:45.079 --> 03:48.041
We can't dispose of it without the owner's permission,

61
03:48.124 --> 03:50.543
but the owner's dead.

62
03:50.626 --> 03:55.131
Vacant properties are a serious problem these days.

63
03:55.214 --> 03:56.549
Right, Minami?

64
03:57.675 --> 04:01.637
You can quickly look up the heir through the online property registry service.

65
04:01.721 --> 04:03.181
Though there is a fee.

66
04:03.264 --> 04:05.099
That's a practicing lawyer for you!

67
04:05.641 --> 04:08.311
Let's find the owner and take him to court. To court!

68
04:08.394 --> 04:10.688
Isn't going to court a bit much?

69
04:10.772 --> 04:14.275
Not at all. Right, Attorney Minami Minamida?

70
04:32.460 --> 04:34.670
Minami, we'll pay your consultation fee.

71
04:35.171 --> 04:37.215
-I won't accept a consultation fee. -But…

72
04:37.298 --> 04:41.552
I submitted my resignation to my supervisor and left the firm.

73
04:42.053 --> 04:45.098
I'm only here because Ririi asked me to come with her.

74
04:45.181 --> 04:48.267
Don't be like that. Your best friend's family needs help.

75
04:49.352 --> 04:50.186
This is it.

76
04:58.111 --> 05:00.780
Oh, sure. Go ahead and remove it if you want.

77
05:00.863 --> 05:04.700
It's been sitting there since my dad died. It's basically junk.

78
05:04.784 --> 05:08.204
Actually, we were hoping you'd arrange to have it removed.

79
05:08.788 --> 05:10.081
-What, us? -Of course.

80
05:11.124 --> 05:12.083
Why?

81
05:12.166 --> 05:15.044
You inherited the construction company's land and building, correct?

82
05:15.128 --> 05:16.671
That junk

83
05:16.754 --> 05:20.383
is between my dad and your family. It has nothing to do with me.

84
05:20.466 --> 05:21.759
It does involve you.

85
05:21.843 --> 05:23.386
-No, it doesn't. -Yes, it does.

86
05:23.469 --> 05:24.720
-No, it doesn't. -Yes, it does!

87
05:24.804 --> 05:25.721
-No! -Yes!

88
05:25.805 --> 05:27.140
No!

89
05:27.223 --> 05:28.850
-It does involve you! -What?

90
05:28.933 --> 05:32.145
Mr. Madoka can exercise his right to reclaim his property.

91
05:32.228 --> 05:33.771
There it is! The right to reclaim it!

92
05:33.855 --> 05:38.609
If someone else's occupation interferes with your ownership, you have the right

93
05:38.693 --> 05:40.862
to demand the property's return.

94
05:40.945 --> 05:44.991
In this case, the storage shed was built on Mr. Madoka's land without permission

95
05:45.074 --> 05:46.742
and occupies that land.

96
05:46.826 --> 05:48.870
As the heir to Tsugihara Construction's

97
05:48.953 --> 05:51.414
land and building, you bear that responsibility.

98
05:51.497 --> 05:54.500
Mr. Madoka has the right to demand that you remove the shed

99
05:54.584 --> 05:55.793
and vacate his land.

100
05:55.877 --> 05:57.920
See? We have the right!

101
05:58.588 --> 05:59.589
Who is this woman?

102
06:01.090 --> 06:04.302
This is Minami Minamida, an attorney.

103
06:04.385 --> 06:07.305
An attorney? Over some junk?

104
06:07.388 --> 06:10.474
I'm only here because Ririi asked me to come…

105
06:10.558 --> 06:13.811
Anyway, it could collapse and hurt someone,

106
06:13.895 --> 06:18.191
so please remove it promptly. Immediately. This second.

107
06:18.274 --> 06:19.817
In this economy?

108
06:20.526 --> 06:22.820
Where am I supposed to get that kind of money?

109
06:23.905 --> 06:25.072
I'm sorry.

110
06:30.620 --> 06:32.079
Minami!

111
06:32.705 --> 06:35.124
I'm so glad you came, Minami.

112
06:39.837 --> 06:42.173
I only explained the right to reclaim property.

113
06:42.256 --> 06:43.758
I wasn't representing you, Ririi.

114
06:43.841 --> 06:47.178
Without that reclaim-whatever you hit him with,

115
06:47.261 --> 06:49.347
he'd have brushed us off.

116
06:49.972 --> 06:53.184
Minami, you really should stay a lawyer.

117
06:53.267 --> 06:54.185
Right, Daddy?

118
06:54.268 --> 06:56.646
Yes. Thank you, Minami.

119
07:00.358 --> 07:02.276
OPEN PREPARING TO OPEN

120
07:03.444 --> 07:04.946
Hello? Anyone here?

121
07:05.029 --> 07:06.239
Yes?

122
07:18.626 --> 07:20.670
CREATIVE ONIGIRI SHOP

123
07:20.753 --> 07:21.587
What do we do?

124
07:22.421 --> 07:23.422
What's wrong?

125
07:23.506 --> 07:25.258
Their lawyer showed up.

126
07:25.341 --> 07:26.217
What?

127
07:32.848 --> 07:34.308
So this is it…

128
07:34.392 --> 07:37.061
Yes. It's been here since around when my daughter was born,

129
07:37.144 --> 07:38.396
so at least 20 years.

130
07:39.605 --> 07:42.483
Were you renting this land to Tsugihara Construction?

131
07:42.567 --> 07:45.361
No. I thought they'd remove it eventually.

132
07:45.444 --> 07:46.571
You never said anything?

133
07:47.196 --> 07:49.991
They were our neighbors. It was awkward.

134
07:50.658 --> 07:51.742
I see.

135
07:52.451 --> 07:56.247
Then they may qualify for adverse possession after 20 years.

136
07:57.164 --> 07:59.208
Adverse possession?

137
07:59.292 --> 08:01.335
If someone openly and peacefully

138
08:01.419 --> 08:04.755
occupies land for a certain period,

139
08:04.839 --> 08:06.841
they can claim ownership of it.

140
08:06.924 --> 08:08.217
Here,

141
08:08.301 --> 08:10.886
the shed has occupied the Madokas' land

142
08:10.970 --> 08:14.640
for over 20 years, satisfying the period

143
08:14.724 --> 08:16.475
required for adverse possession.

144
08:16.559 --> 08:20.062
So the land under the shed becomes theirs?

145
08:20.146 --> 08:22.106
That's not all.

146
08:22.189 --> 08:23.858
If adverse possession is established,

147
08:23.941 --> 08:27.278
ownership passes to the Tsugihara side,

148
08:27.361 --> 08:29.989
so you can no longer demand removal of the shed.

149
08:30.072 --> 08:33.117
They've found a tricky point to use against us.

150
08:33.200 --> 08:34.827
But how is that fair?

151
08:34.910 --> 08:37.163
We let them use our land out of kindness.

152
08:37.246 --> 08:41.000
Apparently, not objecting to their use of the land for 20 years

153
08:41.083 --> 08:43.711
counts as accepting their possession of it.

154
08:43.794 --> 08:45.004
This is the worst.

155
08:45.588 --> 08:47.923
Now Daddy's saying he can't open the cafe

156
08:48.007 --> 08:50.259
with that shed still there.

157
08:50.760 --> 08:52.595
It's my fault.

158
08:52.678 --> 08:55.598
Because I brought up the right to reclaim the property…

159
08:55.681 --> 08:57.642
It's not your fault, Minami.

160
08:57.725 --> 08:59.560
I'm the one who asked you to come.

161
08:59.644 --> 09:02.855
But now that they've hired a lawyer,

162
09:02.938 --> 09:04.940
we need to figure out how to respond.

163
09:06.275 --> 09:07.276
I know!

164
09:07.360 --> 09:09.153
I've stopped being a lawyer,

165
09:09.236 --> 09:12.031
but I know other lawyers. I can introduce you to one, Ririi.

166
09:12.114 --> 09:13.658
You represent me, Minami.

167
09:14.784 --> 09:15.701
No.

168
09:16.202 --> 09:18.829
I can't help you, Ririi.

169
09:22.958 --> 09:24.919
Minami? I'm outside the building.

170
09:25.503 --> 09:27.129
What do I do again?

171
09:27.213 --> 09:29.924
First, check in at the entrance.

172
09:30.007 --> 09:32.218
Right. I just give them your name?

173
09:32.301 --> 09:34.762
No! I've already left the firm.

174
09:34.845 --> 09:36.263
I'm sure it'll still work.

175
09:36.347 --> 09:37.723
Don't use Minami Minamida!

176
09:37.807 --> 09:40.184
I'll try Minami Minamida.

177
09:46.273 --> 09:47.233
Excuse me…

178
09:47.733 --> 09:49.360
Do you know Ms. Minamida?

179
09:50.653 --> 09:51.904
Do you work at the law firm?

180
09:51.987 --> 09:53.155
Yes.

181
09:53.739 --> 09:55.366
Ririi? Are you listening?

182
09:55.449 --> 09:57.535
Don't say Minami Minamida.

183
09:57.618 --> 09:59.412
I'll ask someone here. Never mind.

184
10:05.793 --> 10:06.752
I must decline.

185
10:06.836 --> 10:09.088
-What? Is that a no? -Yes.

186
10:09.171 --> 10:13.759
Minami said this Mr. Miyaji was someone she could sort of recommend.

187
10:23.102 --> 10:26.480
Once adverse possession is established, it's difficult to overturn.

188
10:26.981 --> 10:30.401
If she wants to take a losing case, she should handle it herself.

189
10:30.484 --> 10:31.569
But Minami's already…

190
10:31.652 --> 10:35.322
Resigning doesn't stop her from being a lawyer.

191
10:35.406 --> 10:38.200
What? So Ms. Minamida really did…

192
10:38.284 --> 10:40.536
So that's why she hasn't been coming in.

193
10:41.328 --> 10:42.747
Well…

194
10:42.830 --> 10:43.998
To be precise,

195
10:44.081 --> 10:48.002
she just left a resignation letter on my desk without discussing it with me.

196
10:49.211 --> 10:51.088
Isn't there some way we could help?

197
10:51.172 --> 10:52.131
I'm afraid not.

198
10:57.970 --> 11:00.848
I came all this way for nothing.

199
11:00.931 --> 11:02.933
I'm sorry we couldn't help.

200
11:03.517 --> 11:05.060
Is something wrong?

201
11:06.187 --> 11:07.188
Managing Partner.

202
11:07.730 --> 11:08.564
Managing Partner?

203
11:12.026 --> 11:14.320
-Why not take her case? -But…

204
11:14.403 --> 11:16.822
Ms. Minamida came to us

205
11:16.906 --> 11:18.282
because she trusts the team

206
11:18.365 --> 11:21.285
she worked with, however briefly. Isn't that right?

207
11:21.368 --> 11:22.995
If she trusted us, would she have left

208
11:23.078 --> 11:25.664
without a word to her supervisor or colleagues?

209
11:25.748 --> 11:28.417
She'll tell us when she's ready.

210
11:29.084 --> 11:32.463
We all have strengths and weaknesses. We support each other.

211
11:32.546 --> 11:34.590
Isn't that how a team should work?

212
11:37.551 --> 11:38.844
A team…

213
11:40.387 --> 11:43.390
All right. If you feel that strongly about it.

214
11:44.350 --> 11:46.560
But I have one condition.

215
11:51.065 --> 11:53.526
So why am I the one handling it?

216
11:53.609 --> 11:56.654
Mr. Miyaji and Mr. Himi both seem to have heavy caseloads.

217
11:56.737 --> 11:58.489
I have a pretty heavy caseload myself.

218
11:58.572 --> 11:59.406
Yes.

219
11:59.990 --> 12:03.035
Well, when she became my colleague,

220
12:03.118 --> 12:06.455
I knew she'd give me the runaround sometimes…

221
12:06.956 --> 12:08.666
Suwa, huh…

222
12:09.875 --> 12:11.752
Would you like me to drive you?

223
12:16.340 --> 12:20.135
Suwa… It's a lovely place, isn't it?

224
12:23.138 --> 12:25.307
NEW! AGAR RICE BALLS ¥560 HIGH IN FIBER! HEALTHIER!

225
12:45.494 --> 12:46.453
Minami.

226
12:53.836 --> 12:54.670
Minami!

227
12:56.463 --> 12:59.258
Don't "hm?" me. You're working.

228
13:01.385 --> 13:02.678
If it's on your mind,

229
13:02.761 --> 13:04.972
why don't you join them for the negotiations?

230
13:08.350 --> 13:09.893
I think Ririi would be happy

231
13:09.977 --> 13:12.187
to have you represent her.

232
13:25.576 --> 13:28.621
Were you renting this land to Tsugihara Construction?

233
13:28.704 --> 13:31.790
No. I thought they'd remove it eventually.

234
13:31.874 --> 13:33.000
You never said anything?

235
13:33.083 --> 13:36.045
They were our neighbors. It was awkward.

236
13:37.796 --> 13:40.257
That's my conversation with Mr. Madoka the other day.

237
13:41.050 --> 13:42.343
That's accurate, correct?

238
13:42.968 --> 13:43.927
Yes.

239
13:44.011 --> 13:46.513
So you admit to adverse possession?

240
13:49.016 --> 13:50.309
About that,

241
13:50.893 --> 13:54.396
if you're taking this position

242
13:54.480 --> 13:56.732
because our demand the other day offended you,

243
13:57.232 --> 13:58.484
we apologize.

244
14:02.946 --> 14:05.157
We'll do what we can

245
14:05.240 --> 14:07.951
to help remove the shed.

246
14:08.035 --> 14:10.788
Would you consider withdrawing your adverse possession claim?

247
14:11.538 --> 14:13.624
You'll do what you can?

248
14:15.042 --> 14:15.876
What do you think?

249
14:25.678 --> 14:27.680
What did Ririi say?

250
14:27.763 --> 14:30.349
They wouldn't withdraw their adverse possession claim.

251
14:31.684 --> 14:33.143
I see.

252
14:33.227 --> 14:35.604
Isn't there something we can do?

253
14:35.688 --> 14:40.067
Many people feel too awkward to ask others to return what they've borrowed.

254
14:40.150 --> 14:42.569
Even that jacket I always wear

255
14:42.653 --> 14:44.113
wasn't originally mine.

256
14:44.655 --> 14:47.658
That must've been about 20 years ago, actually.

257
14:47.741 --> 14:50.703
I got drunk at a school reunion and wore it home by mistake.

258
14:50.786 --> 14:52.121
And I've had it ever since.

259
14:52.997 --> 14:55.332
Didn't the owner ask you to return it?

260
14:55.416 --> 14:59.086
No. He'd gone home wearing my leather jacket.

261
15:00.295 --> 15:04.383
So adverse possession applies to both of us, right?

262
15:06.593 --> 15:09.179
Adverse possession applies to both…

263
15:11.390 --> 15:15.269
Could adverse possession apply to the Madokas too,

264
15:15.352 --> 15:16.603
not just them?

265
15:37.583 --> 15:38.792
This is good.

266
15:38.876 --> 15:40.002
Right?

267
15:48.844 --> 15:49.678
Yes.

268
15:49.762 --> 15:53.390
Hello. I'm Makoto, Minami's father.

269
15:54.058 --> 15:54.933
Huh?

270
15:57.102 --> 15:59.897
Civil law recognizes two types of prescription:

271
16:00.439 --> 16:02.816
acquisitive prescription, which grants rights,

272
16:02.900 --> 16:05.277
and extinctive prescription, which extinguishes them.

273
16:06.779 --> 16:07.738
The key here

274
16:07.821 --> 16:10.157
is adverse possession.

275
16:11.366 --> 16:14.244
The key here is adverse possession.

276
16:14.328 --> 16:16.538
This is way too much hassle!

277
16:16.622 --> 16:17.623
Um…

278
16:18.791 --> 16:19.833
Do it yourself!

279
16:19.917 --> 16:21.251
But I…

280
16:21.335 --> 16:23.712
Just talk to her yourself! Come on!

281
16:23.796 --> 16:24.713
Ms. Minamida?

282
16:30.511 --> 16:31.720
Yes.

283
16:32.387 --> 16:34.181
It's a long shot,

284
16:34.264 --> 16:36.600
but there may be a way to make this work.

285
16:40.062 --> 16:42.356
Mr. Tsugihara has acquired the Madokas' land

286
16:42.439 --> 16:45.359
by adverse possession

287
16:45.442 --> 16:47.653
through continuing to occupy it as his own.

288
16:48.487 --> 16:52.366
But couldn't the same argument work the other way around?

289
16:53.117 --> 16:54.034
The other way around?

290
16:54.118 --> 16:58.038
In other words, we could argue that the Madokas

291
16:58.122 --> 17:01.834
have possessed the shed on their land for 20 years.

292
17:03.001 --> 17:04.795
I see.

293
17:04.878 --> 17:07.297
If the shed belongs to the Madokas,

294
17:07.381 --> 17:11.135
Mr. Tsugihara would no longer have grounds to claim the land as his own.

295
17:11.218 --> 17:12.386
Yes.

296
17:12.469 --> 17:16.557
The Madokas would have to dispose of the shed themselves,

297
17:16.640 --> 17:18.976
but they could avoid losing their land.

298
17:19.852 --> 17:22.062
That may work in theory,

299
17:22.146 --> 17:25.065
but both sides would be using the same law in the same dispute.

300
17:25.149 --> 17:27.276
One would claim the land,

301
17:27.359 --> 17:29.903
and the other the shed.

302
17:29.987 --> 17:32.197
Which claim would prevail?

303
17:32.865 --> 17:34.324
Probably

304
17:34.408 --> 17:38.036
whichever side can provide clearer evidence of possession.

305
17:38.620 --> 17:42.958
What would prove they've possessed the shed for 20 years?

306
17:44.251 --> 17:45.544
That would be…

307
17:49.590 --> 17:51.300
The agar!

308
17:52.176 --> 17:53.218
Yes!

309
17:53.302 --> 17:54.887
Every year, Ririi's mother

310
17:54.970 --> 17:56.763
dried seaweed on the shed's roof

311
17:56.847 --> 17:58.849
to make her own agar.

312
17:58.932 --> 18:03.353
That would support the Madokas' claim to 20 years' possession of the shed.

313
18:03.437 --> 18:04.730
She did! Every year!

314
18:04.813 --> 18:06.565
Can you prove that?

315
18:06.648 --> 18:10.194
Are there any photos, or perhaps entries in your mother's diary?

316
18:10.277 --> 18:13.030
My parents aren't the type to take photos or keep diaries.

317
18:17.409 --> 18:18.452
What about sketches?

318
18:22.206 --> 18:24.499
I've loved drawing since I was little.

319
18:24.583 --> 18:26.335
I used to draw the garden a lot.

320
18:26.418 --> 18:29.254
Wow, these are good!

321
18:30.672 --> 18:33.842
It's amazing what your parents keep.

322
18:38.639 --> 18:42.851
You can go help Ririi, you know.

323
18:47.522 --> 18:49.608
I have to help here at the shop.

324
18:56.657 --> 18:59.159
I think there are more of Ririi's drawings upstairs.

325
18:59.243 --> 19:00.786
Could we see them?

326
19:00.869 --> 19:01.954
Please.

327
19:11.171 --> 19:13.465
Um, is the person in this drawing…?

328
19:14.758 --> 19:16.885
Yeah, that's Minami in middle school.

329
19:16.969 --> 19:18.595
Oh, wow.

330
19:19.596 --> 19:23.016
What was Ms. Minamida like back then?

331
19:23.725 --> 19:26.395
The kids in our class called her "Miss Okay."

332
19:26.979 --> 19:28.188
"Miss Okay"?

333
19:29.606 --> 19:31.275
Minami transferred to our school…

334
19:31.358 --> 19:35.362
I'd like to introduce a student who's joining our class today.

335
19:35.445 --> 19:37.322
Could you introduce yourself?

336
19:37.406 --> 19:41.952
Yes! Forwards or backwards, I'm Minami Minamida!

337
19:42.035 --> 19:43.954
Kayak, deed… Oh…

338
19:44.663 --> 19:45.497
What's wrong?

339
19:46.081 --> 19:48.208
My father told me not to say

340
19:48.292 --> 19:52.921
anything unnecessary when introducing myself at my new school, but I did.

341
19:54.798 --> 19:56.675
All right, quiet down!

342
19:57.259 --> 19:59.720
Minamida, take that seat over there.

343
19:59.803 --> 20:01.054
Yes.

344
20:01.972 --> 20:03.974
All right, settle down.

345
20:04.683 --> 20:05.934
Let's start homeroom.

346
20:06.018 --> 20:09.187
At first, I just thought the new girl seemed kind of slow.

347
20:12.190 --> 20:14.109
She was always falling over.

348
20:17.988 --> 20:19.906
Huh? What happened?

349
20:19.990 --> 20:22.826
Hey, Minamida, are you okay?

350
20:23.660 --> 20:24.661
Hey…

351
20:25.162 --> 20:26.246
I'm okay…

352
20:27.706 --> 20:28.957
And bumping into things.

353
20:36.923 --> 20:38.633
That must hurt!

354
20:38.717 --> 20:39.885
Are you okay?

355
20:39.968 --> 20:41.219
I'm okay.

356
20:42.012 --> 20:43.221
Come on, let's go.

357
20:45.349 --> 20:49.311
She always echoed "okay," so they called her "Miss Okay."

358
20:50.771 --> 20:53.315
But I hadn't realized.

359
20:58.153 --> 21:00.364
What will she say if someone bumps into her?

360
21:01.865 --> 21:02.908
Let's find out.

361
21:02.991 --> 21:03.992
Go for it!

362
21:09.664 --> 21:12.918
Miss Okay's rice ball rolled away.

363
21:13.585 --> 21:15.212
Are you okay?

364
21:15.295 --> 21:16.546
I'm okay.

365
21:16.630 --> 21:18.131
There she goes again.

366
21:19.049 --> 21:20.384
There she goes again.

367
21:20.467 --> 21:21.510
That's all she can say.

368
21:21.593 --> 21:22.803
She's so freaking funny!

369
21:23.804 --> 21:26.264
It was all just their stupid idea of fun.

370
21:28.642 --> 21:30.310
That was seriously hilarious!

371
21:30.394 --> 21:31.812
You're so good at that!

372
21:31.895 --> 21:33.397
She said she's okay.

373
21:34.439 --> 21:37.275
-What's she gonna do with that rice ball? -Good question!

374
21:43.907 --> 21:47.577
Then I suddenly felt this urge to get some exercise.

375
21:47.661 --> 21:49.079
Oh my god, you're too good.

376
21:49.162 --> 21:50.997
Maybe I'll do it again tomorrow.

377
21:51.081 --> 21:52.457
-That'd be awesome. -Awesome!

378
21:52.541 --> 21:53.625
Right?

379
21:59.631 --> 22:00.882
Hey! What the hell?!

380
22:02.050 --> 22:05.720
You're covered in trash. Are you okay?

381
22:05.804 --> 22:07.222
Are you okay?

382
22:07.305 --> 22:08.598
No, I'm not okay!

383
22:10.058 --> 22:11.893
What the hell are you doing?

384
22:11.977 --> 22:14.146
Stop it! Let go!

385
22:23.947 --> 22:27.701
Time to sweep out the trash!

386
22:40.005 --> 22:41.506
All clean now.

387
22:43.049 --> 22:44.593
All clean now.

388
22:46.052 --> 22:47.846
Then, the next day…

389
23:03.653 --> 23:05.405
You're distracting me. Need something?

390
23:07.908 --> 23:09.951
First period has already started!

391
23:11.328 --> 23:12.537
So?

392
23:37.395 --> 23:39.731
I thought we could walk to school together.

393
23:43.360 --> 23:45.862
I'm safe when I'm with you, Madoka.

394
23:46.738 --> 23:48.657
There's nothing in it for me.

395
24:01.878 --> 24:04.214
Bryde's whales stay upright in the water

396
24:04.297 --> 24:06.299
with their mouths open, waiting for food to enter!

397
24:06.883 --> 24:07.842
Like this.

398
24:10.595 --> 24:12.138
The benefit for you

399
24:12.222 --> 24:15.141
is that I can model for your drawings anytime.

400
24:15.225 --> 24:17.894
Since you don't seem to have any friends at school.

401
24:17.978 --> 24:20.939
I'm alone by choice. It's easier that way.

402
24:25.443 --> 24:28.905
Then I'll be alone with you.

403
24:34.160 --> 24:35.787
You're so weird…

404
24:39.833 --> 24:42.294
Ms. Madoka? Where are you going?

405
24:42.377 --> 24:45.588
Ririi. No "Miss" or anything. Just Ririi.

406
24:45.672 --> 24:47.132
Drop the formalities.

407
24:49.801 --> 24:50.719
Ririi…

408
24:51.261 --> 24:53.763
I'm going to school. Alone.

409
24:53.847 --> 24:55.598
No formalities.

410
24:58.101 --> 24:59.311
Ririi!

411
24:59.394 --> 25:02.897
I shall… I'll come too! Alone.

412
25:07.360 --> 25:09.988
We started hanging out after that.

413
25:10.071 --> 25:12.449
There's never a dull moment with Minami.

414
25:14.326 --> 25:15.327
I know what you mean.

415
25:16.036 --> 25:19.831
I lose track of time when I'm with Ms. Minamida too.

416
25:25.545 --> 25:28.673
Found them! She drew these before elementary school.

417
25:28.757 --> 25:31.009
-Wow! Parents really do keep everything. -Thank you.

418
25:31.092 --> 25:32.719
Have some agar jelly.

419
25:33.803 --> 25:35.847
-Thank you. -Of course.

420
25:35.930 --> 25:38.975
Let's have some agar jelly, then get back to work.

421
25:40.101 --> 25:41.811
Shall we take an agar jelly break?

422
25:42.479 --> 25:43.355
I'll have some.

423
25:43.438 --> 25:45.482
-Looks good! -Thank you.

424
25:46.316 --> 25:47.817
The shed

425
25:47.901 --> 25:50.028
gets just the right amount of sun and airflow.

426
25:50.111 --> 25:52.614
It's the perfect place to dry agar.

427
25:53.615 --> 25:55.450
They shared their agar

428
25:55.533 --> 25:59.245
with your father every year, supporting their claim

429
25:59.329 --> 26:02.165
of peaceful, open possession.

430
26:03.541 --> 26:04.501
But

431
26:05.001 --> 26:09.297
isn't it a stretch to claim 20 years of possession based on a few sketches?

432
26:10.215 --> 26:12.509
Ultimately, that's for the court to decide.

433
26:12.592 --> 26:14.803
Even so, I understand

434
26:14.886 --> 26:18.807
you initially asked Mr. Tsugihara to remove the shed.

435
26:19.391 --> 26:20.392
Yes.

436
26:20.892 --> 26:25.605
Which means you recognized Mr. Tsugihara as its owner, correct?

437
26:25.688 --> 26:29.317
Now you're saying the shed belongs to you.

438
26:30.819 --> 26:32.862
That's a contradiction.

439
26:33.363 --> 26:34.656
You can't change your story now.

440
26:34.739 --> 26:36.282
You did the same thing!

441
26:36.366 --> 26:40.620
Yes. Mr. Tsugihara hadn't mentioned adverse possession then either.

442
26:40.703 --> 26:42.497
You brought a lawyer first!

443
26:42.580 --> 26:44.249
That's why we'd like to revisit…

444
26:44.332 --> 26:45.375
Ms. Asahi!

445
26:46.167 --> 26:47.627
That's enough.

446
26:50.797 --> 26:52.006
Let's put an end to this.

447
27:16.614 --> 27:18.533
So what did Ririi's father decide?

448
27:19.159 --> 27:21.244
He's giving up ownership of the land.

449
27:22.328 --> 27:24.914
Going to court would take time and money.

450
27:24.998 --> 27:26.749
He doesn't want any more conflict.

451
27:28.084 --> 27:30.712
So the shed will stay where it is?

452
27:30.795 --> 27:32.505
Is Ririi okay with that?

453
27:33.298 --> 27:34.340
No…

454
27:36.009 --> 27:38.261
I'm sorry I couldn't help.

455
27:45.727 --> 27:48.771
I'm sorry for all the trouble.

456
27:48.855 --> 27:52.525
We'll update the property registration after the survey.

457
27:52.609 --> 27:54.152
Thank you for handling it.

458
27:59.866 --> 28:01.493
Why are we the ones apologizing?

459
28:07.790 --> 28:09.834
Nothing but junk.

460
28:14.672 --> 28:16.299
Will you clean this up properly?

461
28:24.140 --> 28:25.058
There we go.

462
28:28.102 --> 28:30.230
There.

463
28:30.313 --> 28:31.814
-Let's go. -Right.

464
28:46.913 --> 28:48.331
Ririi, look out!

465
29:02.554 --> 29:03.847
Daddy!

466
29:15.859 --> 29:17.235
-Ririi! -Minami.

467
29:18.111 --> 29:19.654
Are you okay, Mr. Madoka?

468
29:19.737 --> 29:21.948
Sorry I worried you all.

469
29:22.866 --> 29:25.076
Bruised all over. A month to recover.

470
29:25.743 --> 29:27.912
It looks worse than it is. It's nothing serious.

471
29:27.996 --> 29:30.874
What are you talking about? You could've died!

472
29:30.957 --> 29:34.961
Minami, their shed hurt him. We can hold them responsible, right?

473
29:36.254 --> 29:37.130
Well…

474
29:37.213 --> 29:38.381
Just let it go.

475
29:38.464 --> 29:40.592
We're finally close to settling this.

476
29:40.675 --> 29:42.302
We'd only stir things up again.

477
29:42.385 --> 29:43.469
I'm okay.

478
29:43.970 --> 29:45.597
You're not okay!

479
29:45.680 --> 29:47.432
We can't just sweep this under the rug!

480
29:47.515 --> 29:50.310
Ignoring things is what got us into this mess!

481
29:52.061 --> 29:53.187
What about the cafe?

482
29:54.355 --> 29:55.440
It was your dream!

483
29:56.774 --> 29:59.861
I don't want my family getting hurt anymore!

484
30:15.335 --> 30:16.294
Ririi.

485
30:17.545 --> 30:18.588
I…

486
30:24.677 --> 30:25.637
I…

487
30:27.221 --> 30:28.890
I want to help you, Ririi.

488
30:30.016 --> 30:31.893
I want to help your family.

489
30:37.231 --> 30:38.524
Can I do it?

490
30:45.156 --> 30:47.575
Of course you can.

491
30:50.370 --> 30:51.913
Even though I'm autistic?

492
30:53.831 --> 30:57.293
Have I ever cared about that?

493
31:10.014 --> 31:13.309
Please let me represent your family.

494
31:17.689 --> 31:18.898
Dear.

495
31:19.399 --> 31:21.859
Let's face our problems properly.

496
31:22.443 --> 31:24.570
Shouldn't we establish who's responsible,

497
31:24.654 --> 31:27.907
if only to protect the people we care about?

498
31:30.159 --> 31:33.371
I want to put my trust in Minami.

499
31:37.959 --> 31:39.252
You're right.

500
31:41.004 --> 31:42.171
Minami, we'd like your…

501
31:44.090 --> 31:45.925
Huh? Where's Minami?

502
31:59.313 --> 32:00.940
I found something useful.

503
32:01.024 --> 32:02.942
It's thanks to Mr. Madoka getting hurt.

504
32:13.327 --> 32:15.079
The shed collapsed,

505
32:15.163 --> 32:18.624
injuring Mrs. Madoka's husband.

506
32:19.167 --> 32:21.169
Your position was that

507
32:21.252 --> 32:25.173
the shed belonged to you and stood on your land, correct, Mr. Tsugihara?

508
32:26.758 --> 32:30.344
As its owner, you are liable for damage caused by the structure.

509
32:30.428 --> 32:33.306
We will therefore seek Mr. Madoka's medical expenses

510
32:33.389 --> 32:35.266
and compensation for his pain and suffering,

511
32:35.349 --> 32:38.102
as well as compensation for all lost business income

512
32:38.186 --> 32:41.189
resulting from the cafe's opening being delayed by his injuries.

513
32:41.272 --> 32:42.440
Wait, really?

514
32:43.733 --> 32:45.485
-Yes. -What?

515
32:45.985 --> 32:50.907
That's why I told you to remove it promptly. Immediately. That second.

516
32:50.990 --> 32:52.366
You've got to be kidding…

517
32:52.950 --> 32:56.454
As the shed remains at risk of further collapse,

518
32:56.537 --> 32:57.955
we demand its immediate removal.

519
32:58.039 --> 32:59.665
-Also… -There's more?

520
32:59.749 --> 33:03.544
Yes. Earlier, while I was in Mr. Madoka's yard,

521
33:04.796 --> 33:06.380
I found this.

522
33:07.173 --> 33:08.049
What's that?

523
33:08.633 --> 33:12.220
It's the lid of a can of paint used on buildings and similar structures.

524
33:12.303 --> 33:15.807
I found it in the debris and investigated.

525
33:16.974 --> 33:18.226
Please take a look.

526
33:18.768 --> 33:19.727
I found

527
33:19.811 --> 33:21.562
several 18-liter cans of organic solvents.

528
33:21.646 --> 33:22.647
PAINT THINNER

529
33:23.856 --> 33:25.983
Storing these organic solvents requires

530
33:26.067 --> 33:29.487
notification or permits under the Fire Service Act and local ordinances.

531
33:29.570 --> 33:32.406
Failure to comply carries penalties.

532
33:32.490 --> 33:35.576
Did you complete those procedures when you inherited them from your father?

533
33:35.660 --> 33:38.079
Well, no, I…

534
33:38.162 --> 33:40.790
If you pursue your adverse possession claim,

535
33:40.873 --> 33:42.917
we'll have to raise this in court too.

536
33:43.000 --> 33:46.420
Wait! Just a moment!

537
33:46.504 --> 33:47.547
My lawyer said

538
33:47.630 --> 33:50.383
I might get the land without clearing the junk!

539
33:50.466 --> 33:51.551
That's…!

540
33:51.634 --> 33:54.720
Then what will you do about your adverse possession claim?

541
33:56.639 --> 33:57.640
I'll drop it!

542
33:58.141 --> 34:01.769
Just forget the whole thing! I'll clear away the junk too!

543
34:02.436 --> 34:05.273
I see. Understood.

544
34:16.242 --> 34:17.326
Minami.

545
34:20.955 --> 34:22.331
Thank you.

546
34:24.959 --> 34:26.002
Yeah.

547
34:26.085 --> 34:27.670
Minami to the Minamida!

548
34:27.753 --> 34:29.297
Ririi to the Madoka!

549
34:34.468 --> 34:38.681
I'll never forget how you saved my family.

550
34:46.314 --> 34:48.441
Shall we go, then?

551
34:49.025 --> 34:50.943
I've got things to do here. You go ahead.

552
34:51.652 --> 34:52.987
See you, then.

553
34:53.070 --> 34:54.071
See you.

554
34:55.281 --> 34:56.324
Oh, wait a second.

555
34:58.993 --> 35:00.244
Oh… Yes?

556
35:25.394 --> 35:26.520
Shall we go?

557
35:42.828 --> 35:46.999
I hear this area is famous for its beautiful sunsets.

558
35:48.584 --> 35:49.752
Sunsets?

559
35:50.544 --> 35:51.545
I didn't know that.

560
35:53.589 --> 35:54.882
That's strange.

561
35:54.966 --> 35:57.301
That's what Ririi told me…

562
36:04.976 --> 36:06.435
Ms. Minamida.

563
36:09.730 --> 36:11.148
Would you like…

564
36:11.732 --> 36:12.900
to watch the sunset?

565
36:26.789 --> 36:29.625
Do you like sunsets, Minato?

566
36:31.711 --> 36:32.628
Yes.

567
36:33.587 --> 36:35.339
Well, they're beautiful, aren't they?

568
36:39.302 --> 36:40.761
Sunsets look red

569
36:40.845 --> 36:43.014
because the sun is near the horizon.

570
36:43.097 --> 36:46.559
Its light travels through more atmosphere than during the day,

571
36:46.642 --> 36:48.894
so the blue light scatters before reaching us,

572
36:48.978 --> 36:52.565
leaving only the red light to reach us. I read that in a book.

573
36:54.150 --> 36:56.527
I'd never thought about why.

574
36:59.572 --> 37:02.408
It's a big lake, isn't it?

575
37:04.869 --> 37:06.912
Maybe there are whales in it.

576
37:09.957 --> 37:11.334
No, I guess not.

577
37:20.092 --> 37:22.053
Apparently, long before we moved here,

578
37:22.553 --> 37:24.305
you could see sperm whales

579
37:24.388 --> 37:27.058
if you went offshore from my hometown.

580
37:28.225 --> 37:30.353
Have you ever actually seen one?

581
37:30.853 --> 37:32.772
No, I haven't.

582
37:33.314 --> 37:35.733
I don't remember that time either.

583
37:37.234 --> 37:38.277
Someday…

584
37:38.903 --> 37:40.654
I hope you get to see a whale.

585
37:43.324 --> 37:46.160
Yes. I'd like to see one someday.

586
37:53.250 --> 37:54.293
Um…

587
37:55.961 --> 37:57.421
Ms. Minamida.

588
38:01.384 --> 38:04.220
What are you going to do now?

589
38:06.680 --> 38:08.265
Go home by car.

590
38:09.975 --> 38:11.394
That's not what I meant…

591
38:12.770 --> 38:16.941
Are you really… going to stop being a lawyer?

592
38:21.320 --> 38:24.740
Being taken off that last case

593
38:25.574 --> 38:28.452
may have shaken your confidence.

594
38:29.078 --> 38:30.162
But

595
38:31.038 --> 38:35.876
I think you're an excellent lawyer.

596
38:43.259 --> 38:44.844
An excellent lawyer?

597
38:45.344 --> 38:46.971
Why do you think that?

598
38:48.806 --> 38:51.892
You work so hard for your clients

599
38:52.435 --> 38:55.604
that you lose sight of everything else.

600
38:56.647 --> 39:00.901
Well… Sometimes that does worry me.

601
39:03.112 --> 39:05.322
But I'm sure

602
39:05.865 --> 39:10.244
your clients find that incredibly reassuring.

603
39:11.579 --> 39:14.832
I think standing by your clients like that

604
39:15.332 --> 39:18.294
is an important part of being a lawyer.

605
39:33.350 --> 39:34.393
Minato,

606
39:36.187 --> 39:37.730
thank you.

607
39:40.357 --> 39:43.527
I've left the firm,

608
39:44.528 --> 39:46.155
but if there's something I can do,

609
39:46.238 --> 39:49.283
I intend to keep doing my best as a lawyer in my own way.

610
39:51.368 --> 39:52.620
I see.

611
39:53.204 --> 39:54.288
I'm glad…

612
40:00.920 --> 40:01.921
If…

613
40:02.880 --> 40:04.131
If I…

614
40:05.799 --> 40:10.763
If there's anything I can do to help,

615
40:13.015 --> 40:19.563
I'd like to keep supporting you.

616
40:38.832 --> 40:39.667
Come in.

617
40:39.750 --> 40:40.751
Excuse me!

618
40:54.056 --> 40:55.182
It's been a while.

619
40:56.141 --> 40:57.226
It's been a while.

620
40:57.935 --> 41:01.647
I'm glad your friend's problem seems to be resolved.

621
41:02.147 --> 41:03.649
Yes. I'm glad too.

622
41:04.483 --> 41:05.693
So?

623
41:05.776 --> 41:06.735
So?

624
41:08.404 --> 41:10.489
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

625
41:11.865 --> 41:13.534
Isn't this what you came to discuss?

626
41:14.201 --> 41:16.870
Yes. I came to discuss that.

627
41:16.954 --> 41:20.291
Ririi said something about it. Was there a problem with my letter?

628
41:20.791 --> 41:25.713
You can't just leave a resignation letter on your supervisor's desk.

629
41:25.796 --> 41:30.259
I can't process it without speaking to you and confirming your intentions.

630
41:32.136 --> 41:33.887
So? What will you do?

631
41:34.513 --> 41:36.015
Are you really quitting?

632
41:36.098 --> 41:39.810
Does that mean I can still quit quitting?

633
41:39.893 --> 41:42.354
Well, if you quit quitting,

634
41:42.438 --> 41:45.190
I'll deduct those days from your paid leave.

635
41:46.567 --> 41:47.484
Then…

636
41:49.820 --> 41:50.821
I quit!

637
41:53.699 --> 41:55.701
I see. So you're quitting?

638
42:03.375 --> 42:10.341
ATTORNEY MINAMI MINAMIDA

639
42:36.033 --> 42:38.285
How was Ms. Minamida's hometown?

640
42:39.078 --> 42:40.996
It was a long way away.

641
42:43.040 --> 42:45.542
Hey, did you hear anything

642
42:45.626 --> 42:48.629
about her family owning a lot of land or something?

643
42:49.129 --> 42:49.963
No.

644
42:50.047 --> 42:51.256
I see.

645
42:53.467 --> 42:55.010
Why do you ask?

646
42:55.094 --> 42:57.262
Something doesn't sit right

647
42:57.346 --> 42:59.890
about how the managing partner treats Ms. Minamida.

648
42:59.973 --> 43:02.935
The other day, she kept going on about teamwork.

649
43:03.018 --> 43:04.770
That's not like her, is it?

650
43:05.354 --> 43:06.563
Are you jealous?

651
43:06.647 --> 43:07.940
Of course not.

652
43:08.023 --> 43:11.944
She has a disability. I understand making some allowances.

653
43:12.027 --> 43:13.904
But even so…

654
43:13.987 --> 43:19.076
Maybe Ms. Minamida has some seriously powerful connections.

655
43:19.159 --> 43:20.160
Mr. Himi.

656
43:21.662 --> 43:22.955
You must have time to spare.

657
43:25.541 --> 43:26.709
No, I don't!

658
43:26.792 --> 43:29.211
I've got a meeting over a meal with a publisher later!

659
43:29.294 --> 43:30.421
Hello?

660
43:31.046 --> 43:34.675
I thought you might have been looking out for Minami…

661
43:35.342 --> 43:38.220
I'm glad she's decided to stay.

662
43:42.808 --> 43:44.101
You know,

663
43:44.685 --> 43:46.437
I think very highly of her abilities.

664
43:47.020 --> 43:49.857
She seems very persistent with her cases.

665
43:49.940 --> 43:51.608
And she's very creative.

666
43:51.692 --> 43:55.404
I think the other lawyers could learn something from her.

667
43:55.487 --> 43:56.947
I'm glad to hear you say that…

668
43:57.614 --> 44:00.909
But if she ever causes you any trouble,

669
44:01.410 --> 44:03.162
-don't hesitate to tell me. -Don't worry.

670
44:03.245 --> 44:06.457
She may still have a lot to learn,

671
44:06.540 --> 44:08.083
but that will come with time.

672
44:08.959 --> 44:11.503
Don't worry. Leave it to me.

673
44:11.587 --> 44:13.046
Thank you.

674
44:13.714 --> 44:15.424
I can't thank you enough.

675
44:15.507 --> 44:18.260
All right, then. Call me anytime.

676
44:25.184 --> 44:26.226
MINAMI MINAMIDA

677
44:32.816 --> 44:34.026
Like mother, like daughter.

678
44:36.278 --> 44:37.988
She's just like her mother.

679
44:44.870 --> 44:49.875
Subtitle translation by: Hasan Hüseyin Öztürk

680
44:49.958 --> 44:52.794
I'll fight this to the bitter end, however long it takes!

681
44:52.878 --> 44:55.631
Is this really someone who would slander another person?

682
44:55.714 --> 44:58.133
You don't need to do anything this time, Ms. Minamida.

683
44:58.217 --> 44:59.927
I can't let myself fall behind either.

684
45:00.010 --> 45:01.720
You watched the sunset together, right?

685
45:01.803 --> 45:02.846
Tell me!

686
45:02.930 --> 45:04.181
I'm not telling!

687
45:04.890 --> 45:07.059
-Mr. Himi? -Curious?

688
45:09.645 --> 45:12.814
"Minato Funai likes Minami Minamida." Is that true?

689
45:12.898 --> 45:13.899
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
